stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB

    state "Candidate - consent under both regimes" as Candidate
    state "Talent pool - extended consent" as TalentPool
    state "Pre-boarding - consent" as PreBoarding
    state "Employee - basis recorded per regime" as Employee
    state "Purged or erased - tombstone kept" as Purged
    state "Held for a complaint or proceeding" as Held

    [*] --> Candidate: Apply via career site or board ingest, FR-T-X02

    Candidate --> PreBoarding: Offer accepted, FR-T-R54
    Candidate --> TalentPool: Rejected but good, explicit extended re-consent, FR-T-R26
    Candidate --> Purged: Retention horizon reached, no hire, FR-T-X03
    Candidate --> Purged: Consent revoked or erasure request, FR-T-X03
    Candidate --> Held: Complaint opened or notice of proceedings, FR-LEG-026
    Held --> Purged: Hold released by the tenant on counsel instruction

    TalentPool --> Candidate: Re-applies to a new requisition
    TalentPool --> Purged: Extended horizon reached or erasure, FR-T-X03

    PreBoarding --> Employee: Onboarding commit, basis recorded per regime, FR-T-X06
    PreBoarding --> Purged: Offer reneged or withdrawn, then retention horizon, FR-T-X03

    Employee --> [*]: Same person entity persists to payslip N
    Purged --> [*]

    note right of Candidate
        Consent, named purpose and retention horizon
        captured, logged and revocable at application, FR-T-X02.
        Whether the DPDP employment ground, s.7 clause i, reaches
        candidates is a counsel question, so the product never relies on it here.
    end note

    note right of PreBoarding
        Accepted candidate, not yet on the payroll register.
        Still on consent. CTC structure carried forward
        with zero re-keying, FR-T-R54 to FR-T-O01.
    end note

    note right of Employee
        Today the SPDI Rules 2011 require written consent
        for sensitive data such as bank details, for employees too.
        From on or about 13 May 2027 DPDP s.7 clause i may cover
        employment purposes, and the s.8 duties still apply.
        The basis per regime is recorded at each point, FR-T-X06.
    end note
